</div>

They have CSS that includes a small hover animation for turning. Currently the .info class is always displayed (always visible). They want that when hovering, the .info appears on the back of the card (like a flip effect), while the front image becomes blurred to see it more.

They need help adjusting CSS to achieve a flip card effect: front side shows image, back side shows info (text). On hover, the card flips around Y axis, showing the back side (info) with maybe a blur effect on the front image.

We need to propose a solution: Use CSS 3D transforms, set .carte as a container with perspective, position relative. Inside .carte, have two children: .front (image) and .back (info). Initially .back is hidden (maybe via opacity or transform: rotateY(180deg) and opacity: 0). On hover of .carte, apply transform: rotateY(180deg) to .carte, which flips both sides. The .back will become visible (rotateY(180deg) from its initial orientation). Also apply blur filter to the front image during flip: maybe use backdrop-filter: blur(5px) on .front when hovered.

Alternatively, we can keep the structure but add a wrapper for the back side.

Simplify: Provide updated HTML and CSS.

